# Vite loads this on top of `.env` when running `npm run dev`.
#
# The point of the empty value: with no base URL the app issues same-origin
# `/api` requests, which Vite's dev proxy forwards to the backend. That keeps the
# browser's origin and the API's origin identical, so CORS never enters into it.
#
# Setting an absolute URL here instead (as `.env` does, because the Docker image
# build needs one) makes every dev request cross-origin, and the backend's
# CORS_ORIGIN does not list the dev server's port - so the app loads, then fails
# every call, and the session check silently decides you are signed out.
#
# Point the proxy elsewhere with VITE_DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET; see
# docs/reference/environment.md.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
